  "implementation": [
    "Each Runner turn has a fresh SDK invocation ID; business tool context, collector, results, State, metrics and budgets keep the original logical invocation.",
    "Admission checks authorized SDK/session, cancellation, sandbox and original deadline before charging work. Finalizer admission runs in its actual SDK model callback; summarizer has its own checked one-shot callback.",
    "Selected tool-name allowlist precedes telemetry retention. Missing function-call IDs become owned contractor-tool IDs before SDK history projection.",
    "ContractorFunctionTool preserves original int/list[int]/Optional values at the callable preprocessing boundary while retaining structured SDK conversion for other values.",
    "A bounded invocation-local ledger keeps immutable unresolved result snapshots and seals interrupted history through public SessionService after Runner and tools join. Completed results win; never admitted, cancelled and unknown outcomes remain distinct.",
    "Ledger bounds are 10000 cumulative calls, 32MiB pending metadata/JSON, 1001 SDK turns; reconciliation reads at most 2N+3 recent events. Sticky safe failure codes fence the allocation; no callback catch can authorize later work.",
    "Snapshot serialization and lock admission join through cancellation, including repeated cancellation of a returned sibling result. No repair repeats a tool effect or blindly repeats an ambiguous append.",
    "Empty STOP responses retain finite owning outcomes and known usage. A per-turn callback flag preserves MAX_TOKENS even when SDK emits no corresponding event.",
    "Reject ambient optional SDK validation/light-copy/Skill-lifecycle modes. Allocation release clears all three strong callable caches, including the new unwrapped type-hint cache."
  ],
